# Senior Post Fullstack Task Routing

## Purpose

When a user gives feature-level instructions (not explicit API-level instructions), the agent must still complete backend and frontend changes end-to-end with clear contract alignment.

## Mandatory Workflow

1. For mixed feature requests, split work into backend contract/data flow and frontend interaction flow before coding.
2. If frontend depends on a missing/unclear backend interface, define or implement backend contract first, then continue frontend integration.
3. Backend code under `senior-post` must follow `backend-foundation-capabilities` conventions by default.

## Backend Enforcement (senior-post)

- Use request context from `MyRequestContextHolder`; do not parse request manually.
- Follow unified response behavior; do not manually wrap controller returns.
- Use framework exception conventions and align auth/token issues with `85xx`.
- Use `PageQuery` + `PageData` for pagination endpoints.
- Ensure audit fields are handled via auditable domain methods.
- Prefer framework bridge/template components (Feign, Redis template, codegen patterns) over ad-hoc implementations.

## Delivery Requirements

- In implementation responses, explicitly include:
  - backend files changed and why
  - frontend files changed and why
  - API/DTO contract impact
- If only one side is changed, explain why the other side is not required.
